<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Thane T400, the large articulated tractor (D'thorga Farming, batch two; docs/development/farming-batch-two.md, "Tractors"). It
    bends on our own hitch (the owner, 20 Nov 2026): two vehicles of 4 by 4, the front half with the engine and cab driving, the rear half
    with the big rear axle, the linkage and the drawbar following on the articulation pivot with a swing of about 40 degrees [A, a real
    articulated tractor's steering angle, general knowledge]. The rear half's weight is driven grip (drivenAxle), not weight towed. One
    blueprint builds the front, which sets its rear half down behind it and couples it (D'thorga Framework's articulated vehicles); the
    pivot is permanent, with no Unhitch. Two models under one Architect button, from the owner's two pictures: the standard T400 with a
    larger fuel deck, the ballasted T400 B. Its pictures are the whole drawing cut above the hinge (export_farming.py); the pivot sits
    2.31 cells behind the standard front half's middle and 2.39 behind the B's, measured at the cut. Figures authored [A], approximate, in
    the ranges of real articulated tractors (general knowledge, not read from a source). No upgrade tree yet (its icons and overlays come
    in the owner's next paid run). The fuel deck is drawn on the rear half; the fuel is carried by the front, which burns it (a
    simplification). Part keys are saved by position: append only, never reorder. Cells run x -1 to 2, z -1 to 2, the front north.
    Not yet tested in game.
  -->

  <!-- ===== The front half: engine, cab, front axle; it drives. ===== -->
